== Tips and tricks ==

=== Panels on Super ===

Tapping Super (pressing and releasing it alone) shows the panels and the launcher over the dimmed windows, until Escape, a click elsewhere, or switching to a window. To keep the panels hidden the rest of the time, so windows have the whole screen:

{{hc|~/.config/owbox/rc.xml|2=
<owbox>
  <panels>
    <autoHide>yes</autoHide>
    <dim>40</dim>
  </panels>
</owbox>
}}

The binding is an ordinary key binding with the {{ic|tap}} attribute:

 <keybind key="Super_L" tap="yes">
   <action name="TogglePanels"><launcher>owbox-launcher</launcher></action>
 </keybind>

=== Larger decorations ===

{{ic|<owbox><scale>}} draws window frames, menus and popups larger than the theme without making applications larger, which suits Openbox themes on high resolution monitors. owbox Settings sets it under ''Appearance''.

=== Scripting ===

{{ic|owbox --msg}} sends commands to the running owbox: Openbox actions, and lists of the windows, desktops and monitors as JSON. For example:

 $ owbox --msg 'action <action name="GoToDesktop"><to>2</to></action>'
 $ owbox --msg windows

== Troubleshooting ==

=== Screen sharing shows nothing ===

Make sure [[WirePlumber]] is running; without a session manager, PipeWire does not connect the streams.

=== X panels and pagers show no windows ===

X programs such as ''tint2'' cannot see Wayland windows. Use a Wayland panel such as [[Waybar]].

=== Chromium or Electron programs find no keyring ===

Chromium and Electron choose their password store by the desktop's name, and do not know owbox. Start them with {{ic|1=--password-store=gnome-libsecret}}, see [[Chromium#Force a password store]]. When logging in on a text console, add ''pam_gnome_keyring'' to {{ic|/etc/pam.d/login}} to unlock the keyring, see [[GNOME/Keyring#PAM step]].

=== Logging out leaves services failed ===

owbox stops {{ic|owbox-session.target}} when it exits and clears failed user units when it starts. If owbox crashed, run {{ic|systemctl --user reset-failed}}.

